  "details": "In [1220], the position of the on-screen keyboard when activating a `VRC URL Input Field` is sporadically *spatially aware* — This can cause the keyboard to spawn in uncomfortable positions when the space around you is determined to be inadequate for keyboard display.\n**E.G. The keyboard UI may spawn behind you, beside you, at an angle, etc.**\nAdditionally, the keyboard **locks to the HUD** *(that is, the visual display, tracked with head movement)* **when a user is in a station, then activates it.** The keyboard is improperly scaled in this configuration, causing keys to be \"cut off\" towards the edge of the visual display.\n**Potential Fix:**\n- Place Keyboard UI on player's non-dominant hand, similar to the Launchpad/Quick Menu UI. — **E.G. if the player selects an Input Field with their right hand, the keyboard will attach to the left.** — *Dominant hand will be determined based on which hand was used to activate the input field, A.K.A. the active \"pointer\".*\n- If the option to attach menus to HUD is enabled in the Quick Actions menu, the menu will be attached to the HUD **at a reasonable distance as to allow accessible display**. A Movement Bar will be provided to adjust position and scale.\n —\n# Related Feedback\n- [Add the Movement bar to the popup Keyboard](https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1220-add-the-movement-bar-to-the-popup-keyboard)",
